Description:
 ros-jazzy-legged-rl-controllers - Model of legged robot
Changes:
 ros-jazzy-legged-rl-controllers (3.6.0-2026.10.19.06.21) noble; urgency=high
 .
   * Run ONNX inference on the calling thread
     The default intra-op thread pool busy-waits on every core after each run: one policy at 50 Hz kept about
     15 cores busy on a 22-thread machine and starved the simulator and the control loop.
     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <mailto:noreply@anthropic.com>
     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A2pd46YwYV5pUbH2WJmrKG
   * Template RlController on the controller base
     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <mailto:noreply@anthropic.com>
     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A2pd46YwYV5pUbH2WJmrKG
   * Template ControllerBase on the controller interface base
     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <mailto:noreply@anthropic.com>
     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A2pd46YwYV5pUbH2WJmrKG
   * Drop the policy_io publisher
     Sensor data and actuator commands are already published through the
     controller_manager's pal_statistics introspection, so the ad hoc topic
     duplicated them. The parts of the message that introspection does not
     carry yet, the observation vector and the raw actions, will be
     registered into the introspection registry instead.
     Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <mailto:noreply@anthropic.com>
     Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WUhufQkrqJ2LMQEaNq787e
   * Contributors: qiayuanl
